<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37794" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-nosco</span></b> , ĕre, v.
			a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				learn</i> or <i>become acquainted with
			beforehand</i>, <i>to foreknow</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">futura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 38, 82</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18,
				24, 56, § 206</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">promissum sibi caelum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 159</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venturum caeli laborem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 3, 490</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum fata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
					7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 124</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 15, 13</span></i> (but in <i><span class="en">Plaut. As.
				1, 1, 46</span></i>, the correct reading is: in pretio sumus, acc.
			to Fleck. and Ussing).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
